READING
  Representation identity failing proves nothing: two radices spell
  the same quantity with different digits.
  Denoted-value identity is the question. A nonzero DIFFERENT count
  means the two committed arms of this family round the same exact
  sum to different results, so the family compares cost at TWO
  answers rather than at a fixed one.
